From: eelgaev <3100771+eelgaev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-uvm: cancel only the ATS faults on unpopulatable vmas

A GPU fault on a vma that cannot be populated (for example VM_IO) made
uvm_ats_service_faults() return NV_ERR_INVALID_ADDRESS. The replayable
fault path treats any error from it as global and cancels the whole
fault batch.

Treat NV_ERR_INVALID_ADDRESS as an error of those faults only, as later
NVIDIA drivers do: leave them out of the serviced masks so the caller
cancels just them, and continue servicing the rest.

Signed-off-by: eelgaev <3100771+eelgaev@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/nvidia-uvm/uvm_ats_faults.c b/nvidia-uvm/uvm_ats_faults.c
--- a/nvidia-uvm/uvm_ats_faults.c
+++ b/nvidia-uvm/uvm_ats_faults.c
@@ -517,6 +517,15 @@
         UVM_ASSERT((start + length) <= vma->vm_end);
 
         status = service_ats_requests(gpu_va_space, vma, start, length, access_type, service_type, ats_context);
+
+        // A vma that cannot be populated (for example VM_IO) is an error of
+        // these faults only, not a global one. Leave them out of the serviced
+        // masks so the caller cancels just them.
+        if (status == NV_ERR_INVALID_ADDRESS) {
+            status = NV_OK;
+            continue;
+        }
+
         if (status != NV_OK)
             return status;
 
@@ -552,6 +561,15 @@
         UVM_ASSERT((start + length) <= vma->vm_end);
 
         status = service_ats_requests(gpu_va_space, vma, start, length, access_type, service_type, ats_context);
+
+        // A vma that cannot be populated (for example VM_IO) is an error of
+        // these faults only, not a global one. Leave them out of the serviced
+        // masks so the caller cancels just them.
+        if (status == NV_ERR_INVALID_ADDRESS) {
+            status = NV_OK;
+            continue;
+        }
+
         if (status != NV_OK)
             return status;
 
